*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated review artifacts (regenerate via each package's own generator script)
packages/spanish-deck-ui/sample/

# Test output
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Vitest Browser Mode failure attachments (actual/diff screenshots on a
# toMatchScreenshot mismatch) — transient debugging artifacts, never the
# reviewable baseline itself. Baselines live in each test's own
# __screenshots__/ directory, which IS committed.
.vitest-attachments/

# THE OTHER HALF OF THAT RULE, and it took committing the debris twice to see
# it. Vitest also drops a screenshot into __screenshots__/<test file>/ when a
# BROWSER test fails — and that directory is committed on purpose, because it
# is where the visual baselines live. So a failing *.browser.test.ts quietly
# leaves reviewable-looking PNGs beside real baselines.
#
# Only *.visual.test.ts owns baselines. Everything else in there is debris from
# a test that failed on somebody's machine, and three of them reached main
# inside a PR before this line existed.
**/__screenshots__/*.browser.test.ts/

# AND THE THIRD HALF, found while moving the baselines into LFS. The rule above
# ignores a whole BROWSER-test directory, which works because nothing in one is
# ever worth keeping. A VISUAL test directory cannot be ignored that way: the
# baselines live in it. So when a *.visual.test.ts fails, Vitest drops its
# attachment right there, beside the real baselines, matched by no rule at all —
# `git check-ignore -v` finds nothing, and it shows up in `git status` looking
# committable. That is the exact defect the block above was written to fix,
# in the one directory it could not cover.
#
# The discriminator is the NAME, and Vitest is consistent about it: an approved
# baseline is always `<snapshot name>-chromium-linux.png`, while an attachment
# is the full test title plus a retry index. So: ignore the directory's
# contents, then take the baselines back. `.gitattributes` selects the LFS set
# with the same suffix — one fact about Vitest's naming, enforced twice.
**/__screenshots__/*.visual.test.ts/*
!**/__screenshots__/*.visual.test.ts/*-chromium-linux.png

# `pnpm visual:review` renders every screen here for a person to look at.
# Regenerated on demand, never reviewed as a diff, never committed.
visual/review/

